 "readme": "🫀 Heart Disease Prediction Using Deep Autoencoders and Synthetic Data Augmentation\n\nThis project focuses on predicting heart disease using advanced deep learning techniques combined with probabilistic data augmentation.\n\nIt leverages Sparse and Supervised Denoising Autoencoders (DAE) to learn meaningful latent representations from structured medical data. To address data limitations and improve generalization, synthetic data is generated using a Gaussian Copula-based approach.\n\nAn ensemble model is then built by combining latent features from multiple autoencoders, leading to improved predictive performance.\n",
